# Posta — shared Docker build-context excludes (T0.7.1)
#
# The build context for all three app images (apps/{api,worker,web}/Dockerfile)
# is the repo root — each Dockerfile's `pruner` stage needs the whole
# workspace to compute a per-app subset via `turbo prune` (T0.7.3). Without
# this file, `docker build` uploads every one of these directories to the
# daemon on EVERY build, which busts the build cache on any file change at
# all (a touched .md file invalidates the same layers as a source change)
# and, for node_modules especially, makes the context multiple GB.

# --- dependencies & build output --------------------------------------------
# Reinstalled/rebuilt inside the image; never useful from the host. A bare
# `node_modules/` only matches a TOP-LEVEL node_modules — Docker's ignore
# patterns are not recursive like .gitignore's, so every one of these needs
# the `**/` prefix to also catch apps/*/node_modules, apps/web/.next, etc.
**/node_modules/
**/.next/
**/dist/
**/.turbo/
# TypeScript's incremental-build cache (packages/*/tsconfig.json set
# `composite: true`). Discovered the hard way in T0.7.4: a STALE
# .tsbuildinfo left on the host from a local `tsc` run rides along into
# the pruner stage's COPY . . and — because it's gitignored, so a fresh
# clone never has one, but this workstation did — makes `tsc -p
# tsconfig.json` believe the (never-yet-built, in a fresh image) dist/ is
# already up to date and skip emitting it entirely. `tsc` then exits 0
# having produced nothing, and the next workspace package to import it
# fails with "cannot find module" — a confusing failure two stages away
# from the actual cause.
**/*.tsbuildinfo

# --- secrets -----------------------------------------------------------------
# Never bake local credentials into an image layer. `**/` matters here for
# the same reason it does above: an unprefixed `.env.*` only excludes a
# root-level .env — a nested apps/*/.env would ride along into the pruner
# stage's COPY . . otherwise (security review, T0.7.1/T0.7.4).
**/.env
**/.env.*
!.env.example
!**/.env.example

# --- vcs, editor config & docs -----------------------------------------------
.git/
docs/
# A local Claude Code checkout can carry its own config/settings under
# .claude/ at the repo root — never something the image needs, and never
# something that should ride into a build context by accident.
.claude/

# --- data files ----------------------------------------------------------
# GeoIP .mmdb files (S0.7, T0.7.9/10 — a later batch): fetched or baked in
# a dedicated step, never picked up implicitly via the build context.
**/*.mmdb
